# Customer master

The customer record every application reads. One owner writes it; the others read it through the owner's interface.

## Definition

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| customerId | string, 1-12 digits | yes | never reused |
| name | string, up to 100 | yes | |
| status | one of active, suspended, closed | yes | see Codes |
| taxNumber | string | no | class restricted |

## Codes

| Code | Meaning | Since |
| --- | --- | --- |
| active | the customer may be invoiced | - |
| suspended | no new invoices; open ones stay | - |
| closed | no activity; kept for the retention period | - |

## Ownership and access

| Who | May |
| --- | --- |
| customer data team | create and change |
| billing-web | read |

## Rules

| Id | Rule | Source |
| --- | --- | --- |
| SD-01 | A customer is closed only when it has no open invoice | <!-- RULE id in the legacy specification --> |

